WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.580
In the 1970s and 1980s, people put blue catfish into Virginia's rivers.

2
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.200
Blue catfish come from the Mississippi River basin.

3
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.460
Today they are common in parts of those rivers.

4
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.860
So what happens to a river when people bring in a big new fish?

5
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:24.793
People are part of ecosystems.

6
00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:28.813
We depend on them for food, water and energy.

7
00:00:29.813 --> 00:00:34.473
A habitat is the place where an organism finds food, water and shelter.

8
00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:40.873
A population is all members of one species in one area at one time.

9
00:00:42.093 --> 00:00:46.893
Land use is how people use land, like farms, homes or roads.

10
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:53.027
Taking resources, like wood or gravel, changes habitats too.

11
00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:58.707
Habitat destruction is damage that removes or ruins a habitat.

12
00:00:59.707 --> 00:01:02.687
Filling in a marsh to build homes is one example.

13
00:01:03.707 --> 00:01:08.187
Animals there must move or die, so their populations often drop.

14
00:01:09.447 --> 00:01:13.847
Pollution is harmful material added to air, water or soil.

15
00:01:13.847 --> 00:01:18.647
Extra fertilizer in a river can feed fast algae growth.

16
00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:24.647
A native species lives in a place naturally, without people bringing it.

17
00:01:25.187 --> 00:01:28.107
White catfish are native to Virginia's Bay rivers.

18
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:34.927
An invasive species is brought to a new place, spreads and harms native species.

19
00:01:36.027 --> 00:01:37.387
Being new is not enough.

20
00:01:37.887 --> 00:01:39.927
It must spread and cause harm.

21
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.080
Competition is when species need the same resource and there is not enough.

22
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.900
It does not need a fight.

23
00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.500
Blue catfish eat fish and sometimes blue crabs.

24
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.600
Scientists report white catfish eat similar prey.

25
00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.260
So the two may compete for food.

26
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.460
If blue catfish eat many of these, less is left for white catfish.

27
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:09.003
A food web links species by who eats whom.

28
00:02:09.563 --> 00:02:13.643
So a change in one population can spread through the whole web.

29
00:02:14.643 --> 00:02:17.623
Suppose blue catfish eat many blue crabs.

30
00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:21.983
Then fewer may be left for other crab eaters, including people.

31
00:02:22.883 --> 00:02:26.323
So what happens when people bring in a big new fish?

32
00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:29.843
Some populations go up, and others go down.

33
00:02:30.403 --> 00:02:32.503
The change spreads through the food web.
